<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<TestCaseEntity>
   <description>Verifies old UI's postal code rules (confirmed live 9/17/2026):
- Blank + Submit shows "zip code can't be blank"
- Field has maxlength="15" HTML attribute — this caps input directly rather
  than triggering an error message, so ">15 characters" can't actually be
  entered through normal typing. "Maximum 15 characters" in the UI is a
  static hint, not a dynamically-triggered error.

Contrast with new UI, which enforces neither the blank check via error text
(uses disabled button instead) nor any max length at all — see
TC_Registration_InvalidPostalCode.</description>
   <name>TC_Registration_InvalidPostalCode_OldUI</name>
   <tag></tag>
   <comment></comment>
   <recordOption>OTHER</recordOption>
